# Stage 2: Data Sync Strategy Implementation Plan

This stage focuses on making the system awareness of data freshness visible to both the user and the AI.

## Proposed Changes

### Backend: Freshness Tracking

#### [NEW] [sync_log.py](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/models/sync_log.py)
Create a new model to track individual sync runs.
- [id](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/lib/UIContextProvider.tsx#49-65), `user_id`, `source` (canvas/ics/craft), `status` (success/failed), `started_at`, `duration_ms`, `details` (JSON).

#### [MODIFY] [database.py](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/database.py)
- Register `SyncLog` model for initialization.

#### [NEW] [sync.py](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/routers/sync.py)
Create a new router for sync operations and freshness status.
- `GET /api/v1/sync/freshness`: Returns age of last sync for all modules.
- `POST /api/v1/sync/canvas`: Trigger a manual sync.

#### [MODIFY] [canvas_sync.py](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/services/canvas_sync.py)
- Update [sync_all](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/services/canvas_sync.py#355-412) to create a `SyncLog` entry upon completion.

---

### Frontend: Visual Indicators

#### [NEW] [SyncIndicator.tsx](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/components/chat/SyncIndicator.tsx)
Create a small, status-dot component for the chat panel.
- Green: < 5 mins
- Yellow: 5-30 mins
- Amber: 30-60 mins
- Red: > 60 mins (plus a "Sync Now" link)

#### [MODIFY] [DailyBriefChat.tsx](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/components/chat/DailyBriefChat.tsx)
- Embed `SyncIndicator` in the chat header.

